  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Weldy Lamont Rural Electrification Project, through Weldy Lamont Associates, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A proposed USTDA de minimis training grant would support a bid by the U.S. company Weldy Lamont Associates, Inc. to provide equipment and services to expand energy access in Senegal through grid extension and off-grid renewable solutions. The proposed grant would be provided to the Senegalese Ministry of Energy. The training supported by this grant would help increase Senegal&apos;s capacity to implement, operate and maintain the technology and systems required to expand energy access to rural communities in Senegal.</narrative>
  </description>
